{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unaroused-undead-ibisbill","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Escaped-bug analysis (ticket cranial-goodly-seahog) found ~4 regressions from new CI gates/floors/caps that break in-flight or pre-gate branches: medium-loved-newt (Git-floor gate hard-fails in-flight changes), impudent-sodium-ferret (new-gate steps fail pre-gate changes), rancid-aerophobic-skylark (module-size cap breaks main), brattish-ladyish-jaguar (unguarded gate steps; a correct finding was DROPPED). Add a ci-gate-compat criterion scoped to .github/workflows/** + gate scripts: a new hard-fail gate must guard/grandfather in-flight and pre-gate branches. Advisory first.","id":"6f2e-58a5-dfac-42f3","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Add code-review ci-gate-compat criterion (new hard-fail gates must grandfather in-flight branches)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787070688198138001,"uuid":"0947cee1-a3fa-4dbe-80f2-014e1f7c40ea"}